this bus is evacuating the first batch  of chinese citizens from ukraine  chinese state media say the group of 600  people mostly students have been taken  from the cities of kiev and odessa to  neighboring moldova  but many others have been left behind  zhang dongsha has been frantically  packing his bags and plans to catch a  train to ukraine's west from the eastern  city of denipro where he studies  it's hard for us to fall asleep at night  because you're always afraid  and the air defense sirens keep going  off  he says the chinese embassy has been  concentrating on evacuating people from  areas affected by fighting but he's  worried the conflict will soon reach  denipro more than 6 000 chinese  nationals in ukraine are trying to leave  they're being encouraged to take trains  to neighbouring countries chartered  flights are also planned  the current situation is complex and  volatile the foreign ministry and the  chinese embassy in ukraine are closely  following the situation and studying all  possible ways to assist chinese citizens  to evacuate voluntarily and safely  despite chinese students and workers  expressing concerns about their safety  online it's taken longer for china to  pull its people out than other countries  beijing has close ties with moscow and  has refused to condemn the russian  attack  instead blaming nato and the us for  increasing tensions  state media has downplayed reports of  destruction in ukraine calling the  invasion a special military operation  some social media users have posted  comments in favor of russian president  vladimir putin supporting what they say  is his war against the west  china's foreign ministry says its  strategic partners with russia not  allies it cannot afford to offend moscow  but has also emphasized its friendly  relationship with kiev china is  ukraine's number one trading partner and  a major source of foreign investment  jiangdong says the perception that china  backs russia has stoked anti-chinese  sentiment there  ukrainians have a bad impression of the  chinese and some may be anti-china if  your family members join the army or die  and they think china supports russia it  makes me feel scared so i didn't want to  stay i want to leave last week chinese  citizens were advised to display their  national flag when traveling as a safety  precaution  the chinese officials reversed that  instruction a day later saying they  should be careful when revealing their  nationality katrina u al jazeera beijing
 

